    sectors="Services 61%, Industry 36%, Agriculture 3%",
    industries=["Automotive manufacturing (undisputed world champion in cars produced per capita: over 1 million vehicles produced annually across four major auto plants: Volkswagen Slovakia in Bratislava, Stellantis in Trnava, Kia Motors in Žilina, Jaguar Land Rover in Nitra, plus the new Volvo Cars all-electric megasite in Košice)", "Information technology and cybersecurity (ESET - global cybersecurity titan and maker of NOD32 antivirus; Pixel Federation - game software)", "Electrical engineering and consumer electronics (Samsung Electronics, Foxconn)", "Metallurgy and steel production (U.S. Steel Košice - major blast furnace steel complex)", "Machinery, industrial robotics, and defense equipment (ZVS Holding, Konstrukta Defence - Zuzana howitzers)", "Chemicals, plastics, and pharmaceutical manufacturing (Slovnaft oil refinery, Duslo Šaľa)"],
    agriculture=["Wheat, barley (malting barley for brewing), and maize / corn in the southern Danubian lowlands", "Sugar beets and sunflowers", "Oilseed rape / Canola", "Dairy farming and sheep breeding (world-famous Bryndza sheep cheese)", "Wine viticulture (Small Carpathian wine region, Tokaj region shared with Hungary)", "Forestry and timber processing"],
